# Build output
/dist/
/plumbline
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# Bundles and reports — these contain host inventory and must never be
# committed by accident.
*.plb
*.plb.sig
# The golden bundles are the one exception, and they are exempt by name rather
# than by living under testdata/: they are recorded from stock container images,
# scrubbed by tools/goldenrecord, and committed on purpose (docs/FIXTURES.md §6).
# A bundle that lands anywhere else is still an accident.
!testdata/bundles/*.plb
plumbline-report-*.json

# Any SARIF, wherever it lands. `plumbline scan --format sarif -o out.sarif` is
# the first thing anyone tries when wiring up code scanning, and the file it
# writes is a report about a real host — the same reconnaissance a bundle is.
# No .sarif is checked in and none should be; the corpus that CI re-evaluates
# is testdata/bundles.
*.sarif

# Suppression files. These name check IDs, subjects and fingerprints from a
# real host, and the justification field is free text somebody wrote about
# their own infrastructure. An operator keeps theirs in their own repository,
# not in this one.
suppress.json
suppressions.json
plumbline-suppress*.json

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local
.env
*.local.yaml
